<Prose
  title="Returns & exchanges"
  description="How to exchange or return a PB&B order. The first exchange on any order is free."
  heading="Returns & exchanges"
  standfirst="Fit is the main reason clothing gets sent back, so exchanges are built to be easy rather than discouraged."
  updated="[CONFIRM] date"
>
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      <strong>The short version:</strong> if the size is wrong, send it back and we'll swap it. Your
      first exchange on an order costs you nothing.
    </p>
  </blockquote>

  <h2>Exchanges</h2>
  <p>
    If something doesn't fit, you can exchange it for a different size or a different colourway of
    the same garment within <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM] 30 days</mark> of delivery. We cover
    return shipping on the first exchange of any order, and we ship the replacement at no extra
    cost.
  </p>
  <p>
    If the size you want has sold out by the time we receive your return, we'll offer you the choice
    of a refund or store credit — we won't hold your money waiting on a restock.
  </p>

  <h2>Returns for refund</h2>
  <p>
    Unworn, unwashed items with tags attached can be returned for a refund within
    <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM] 30 days</mark> of delivery.
    <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM]</mark> whether the customer or PB&amp;B pays return shipping on a
    refund (as opposed to an exchange) — this is the single most important number to set, and it is
    deliberately left blank rather than guessed.
  </p>
  <p>Refunds go back to the original payment method within 5–10 business days of us receiving the item.</p>

  <h2>Condition</h2>
  <p>To be accepted, an item needs to come back:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Unworn and unwashed, with the original tags still attached</li>
    <li>Free of smoke, fragrance, deodorant marks and pet hair</li>
    <li>In or with its original packaging where practical</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We check every return. If something comes back visibly worn we'll contact you before making a
    decision rather than silently rejecting it.
  </p>

  <h2>Final sale</h2>
  <p>
    <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM]</mark> Whether anything is final sale — typically sale items,
    seconds, or stickers and other small accessories. If nothing is final sale, say so explicitly
    here, because shoppers look for it.
  </p>

  <h2>Faulty or wrong items</h2>
  <p>
    If a print is misplaced, a seam fails, or we sent the wrong thing, that is on us: email
    <a href="/contact">support</a> with your order number and a photo within
    <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM] 30 days</mark> and we'll replace it or refund it in full,
    including shipping both ways. This applies regardless of the standard return window.
  </p>

  <h2>How to start a return</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Email <a href="/contact">support</a> with your order number and what you'd like to do.</li>
    <li>We'll send a return label and the address.</li>
    <li>Pack the item with its tags and drop it off.</li>
    <li>We process it within 3 business days of arrival and email you when it's done.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>International returns</h2>
  <p>
    <mark class="todo">[CONFIRM]</mark> Whether international returns are accepted, who pays the
    shipping, and whether duties already paid are refundable.
  </p>

  <h2>Your statutory rights</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing in this policy limits any rights you have under consumer law in your country. Where
    local law gives you a longer window or better terms than the above, local law applies.
  </p>
</Prose>
